{
  "Version": "2012-10-17",
  "Statement": [
    {
      "Sid": "DenyDisableCloudTrail",
      "Effect": "Deny",
      "Action": [
        "cloudtrail:StopLogging",
        "cloudtrail:DeleteTrail",
        "cloudtrail:UpdateTrail"
      ],
      "Resource": "*"
    }
  ]
}

/*
  WHY THIS SCP EXISTS:
  CloudTrail is the primary audit log for every AWS account.
  It records every API call — who did what, when, and from where.

  This SCP prevents:
  - StopLogging: pausing the trail (creates a gap in the audit record)
  - DeleteTrail: permanently removing the trail configuration
  - UpdateTrail: redirecting logs to an attacker-controlled S3 bucket
    (the least obvious attack — logging appears active but goes elsewhere)

  Attach at Root level. No OU or member account root user can override it.
  Satisfies ISO 27001, SOC 2, CBN IT risk management, and POPIA requirements
  for immutable audit logs.

  NOTE: This SCP does not restrict the Management Account.
  Protect the Management Account's CloudTrail separately via IAM policies.
*/
